e** — say 100, which is the minimum raise allowed (valid actions include 100 or more).\n\nWhy not check? Because if you check, opponent might check back with worse hands (like top pair A-x), and you win, but you gain no value. Or they might bluff with air — but safer to bet and get value from weaker pairs or draws.\n\nWhy not go all-in? Too risky — if opponent has flush, they’ll call and beat you. If they have K-J, they’ll call. So better to bet small and get calls from worse hands.\n\nFold? No — you have a made straight.\n\nCheck? Possible, but suboptimal — you want to build pot with a strong hand.\n\nSo best: **bet 100** — small value bet.\n\nReason:  \nYou have a Queen-high straight, which is strong on this board. Opponent showed weakness by checking twice. A small bet of 100 can extract value from weaker hands (like top pair, two pair, or jack-high straight) while minimizing risk against stronger hands like flushes or K-J. Going all-in risks too much; checking forfeits value. Hence, a minimal raise is optimal.\n\nAnswer: 100"}
